MID_EV13_057_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_057_m01_001: Bonaventure, how long do we have until the Mosa\nmake their next move?
MID_EV13_057_m01_002: The full picture is not yet clear to me, but I doubt we\nhave the luxury of time.
MID_EV13_057_m01_003: The Mosa's defenses will no doubt be complete in\nanother month, making retaliation more difficult.
MID_EV13_057_m01_004: Should they push past Grania Stronghold, Saramis\nwill be left utterly defenseless.
MID_EV13_057_m01_005: In that light, I should like to return to Megaira before\nthe Mosa make any new moves.
MID_EV13_057_m01_006: Then it will be critical to take the most direct route.
MID_EV13_057_m01_007: Departing from Dagsion, we can take the ocean\ncurrents east from Socie Bay to Callianeira Port.
MID_EV13_057_m01_008: Then we can tack south for two days while riding the\ncurrents to end up here. It is a good season for it.
MID_EV13_057_m01_009: Catching the trade winds here would allow us to\nmake quick landfall at Megaira. What say you?
MID_EV13_057_m01_010: It is a sound plan...with a problem. This route will\ntake us far from the coast.
MID_EV13_057_m01_011: The soldiers of Saramis come from nautical stock,\nbut the Trafalgar is a galley with a shallow draft.
MID_EV13_057_m01_012: In a serious storm, she'll capsize and send us all\nto the depths.
MID_EV13_057_m01_013: The uprising is a grave matter, but graver still would\nbe the loss of Your Majesty.
MID_EV13_057_m01_014: <NCA>Consider the plan.
MID_EV13_057_m01_015: <NCB>Look to Bonaventure.
MID_EV13_057_m01_016: <ACA>Had I known this would happen, I would have\nchartered the Galicia rather than the Trafalgar.
MID_EV13_057_m01_017: <ACA>The Galicia out of Alecto is a galleon. For this plan,\nit is indeed better for a voyage far out to sea.
MID_EV13_057_m01_018: <ACA>But it has a deeper draft and never would have\ncarried us here up the shallow Talto River.
MID_EV13_057_m01_019: <ACA>No, I believe the Trafalgar was our only choice\nunder the circumstances.
MID_EV13_057_m01_020: Personally, I would suggest a more direct course to\nMegaira rather than rely on navigational tricks.
MID_EV13_057_m01_021: The currents may pose a challenge, but with the right\nrigging, we could benefit from the wind at our backs.
MID_EV13_057_m01_022: With minimal supplies to lighten the weight...\nrotating the rowers...and sailing without cease...
MID_EV13_057_m01_023: we should be able to return before the fighting\nstarts at the least risk to ourselves.
MID_EV13_057_m01_024: If that is our only course of action, then so be it.\nNow, let us make our report to the Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV13_058_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_058_m01_001: Thank you for receiving us on such short notice.
MID_EV13_058_m01_002: When one of your stature requests an audience so\nurgently, I take heed.
MID_EV13_058_m01_003: Come now. Meet my eyes, and tell me what has\nhappened.
MID_EV13_058_m01_004: I shall say it straight. The Mosa have taken\nFort Zanbar.
MID_EV13_058_m01_005: It seems that they were waiting for my prolonged\nabsence before they struck.
MID_EV13_058_m01_006: Fort Zanbar? If I recall, that is the bastion on the\nfront lines of the new region of Ogmios.
MID_EV13_058_m01_007: Yes. It is the linchpin of our defense against the\nMosa. To have it taken from us is a bitter blow.
MID_EV13_058_m01_008: Therefore, we mean to return to Megaira at once\nto recapture the fortress.
MID_EV13_058_m01_009: While I wish it were not necessary, I must withdraw\nfrom the Heroic Games.
MID_EV13_058_m01_010: That is unfortunate...but I understand. You have\nmade the right decision, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV13_058_m01_011: The peace of the Dagdan Empire relies on your work\nas our shield against Southern Dagda.
MID_EV13_058_m01_012: I regret that you will not be able to advance further\nin the games, but that is a trivial concern.
MID_EV13_058_m01_013: Queen Theodora, I will pray with all my heart that\nyour struggle ends in victory.
MID_EV13_058_m01_014: Yes, my lord. I value your kind words.
MID_EV13_058_m01_015: I offer you a proposition before you go.
MID_EV13_058_m01_016: You have expressed to me the boon you would\nhave sought here.
MID_EV13_058_m01_017: I will consider granting it if you manage to retake\nFort Zanbar.
MID_EV13_058_m01_018: You will?! Truly? If so, then I shall not rest until\nit is done.
MID_EV13_058_m01_019: I vow to repay you for your generosity in this matter.
MID_EV13_058_m01_020: Under the circumstances, you may also access the\nGate of the Gods in the temple of Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_058_m01_021: Through it, you can travel from Dagsion to the\ntemple of Yu Phas in Cybele instantaneously.
MID_EV13_058_m01_022: One hopes that this will shorten your itinerary.
MID_EV13_058_m01_023: After all, time is of the essence, yes? I would be\nremiss not to help where I can.
MID_EV13_058_m01_024: That would be akin to a miracle for us. We shall\ngladly accept your offer.
MID_EV13_058_m01_025: It cannot transport your entire force, but a small\ngroup can use it with ease.
MID_EV13_058_m01_027: I will speak with the gatekeeper. Visit the temple\nwhen you are prepared to leave.
MID_EV13_059_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_059_m01_001: So this is the Gate that should take us to the temple\nof Yu Phas in the dead city Ahm Lu.
MID_EV13_059_m01_002: I have never laid eyes on one before. They are\ntypically reserved for the gods.
MID_EV13_059_m01_003: Is this a gate or a bunch of light? Didn't realize the\nthing would be so fancy.
MID_EV13_059_m01_004: Uh, Queen Theodora, are you sure this is OK?
MID_EV13_059_m01_005: Worry not. We have the Divine Sovereign's express\npermission.
MID_EV13_059_m01_006: Not what I meant. The one in the temple on the\nother end hasn't been used in centuries, right?
MID_EV13_059_m01_007: I don't like it at all. You're gonna have to pony up to\nget me on board for this one.
MID_EV13_059_m01_008: Lilian! Our nation is in crisis! Can you put your\navarice aside for one second?!
MID_EV13_059_m01_009: No. Money is the great motivator.
MID_EV13_059_m01_010: I understand. I will consider it after the current\ncrisis is dealt with.
MID_EV13_059_m01_011: Now, enough chatter. We must move swiftly. Enter\nthe circle etched into the ground.
MID_EV13_059_m01_012: <NCA>Examine your surroundings.
MID_EV13_059_m01_013: Hm? Have we arrived already?
MID_EV13_059_m01_014: Hey, look at that! Everything around us changed\nin the time it took to blink!
MID_EV13_059_m01_015: It worked? Everyone's here in one piece? Well, that's\na start.
MID_EV13_059_m01_016: Incredible. If we could transport all our soldiers this\nway, it would change the face of war.
MID_EV13_059_m01_017: Do you see that, Your Majesty? It is the Isle of Balor.
MID_EV13_059_m01_018: A sure sign that we are indeed at Yu Phas's\ntemple in Ahm Lu.
MID_EV13_059_m01_019: Even knowing this is the workings of the gods, it is\nstill breathtaking to experience.
MID_EV13_059_m01_020: Hey, does it feel really strange here to anyone else?
MID_EV13_059_m01_021: For some reason I haven't stopped shivering since\nwe got here.
MID_EV13_059_m01_022: I feel a tingle in my spine as well. And I seem to\nhave a sudden case of goose bumps.
MID_EV13_059_m01_023: Is there something here invisible to the eye?
MID_EV13_059_m01_024: I believe I see now why the Divine Sovereign was\napprehensive about this place.
MID_EV13_059_m01_025: The unusual air here has grown heavier than I recall\nfrom sneaking in long ago.
MID_EV13_059_m01_026: Even if we are awarded this land, can it be restored\nto a state fit for human habitation?
MID_EV13_060_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_060_m01_001: I bear a message for Prince Dyan. Queen Theodora\nhas reportedly returned to Megaira.
MID_EV13_060_m01_002: Faster than I expected. Soon that woman will see\nwhich of us is truly worthy of the throne.
MID_EV13_060_m01_003: "Faster than expected" is an understatement. This\nwas not the plan! We were meant to have more time!
MID_EV13_060_m01_004: Silence! Remind me who gift wrapped this so-called\nimpregnable fortress for you?
MID_EV13_060_m01_005: It was my genius that restored to you what was taken\nin the War of Grania.
MID_EV13_060_m01_006: But now it will be even more difficult getting past\nGrania Stronghold, let alone marching on Megaira.
MID_EV13_060_m01_007: There is no need for that. Your fixation on these\nthings is why you will always be our inferiors.
MID_EV13_060_m01_008: What did you say?
MID_EV13_060_m01_009: My goal, now and always, has been to take that\nwoman's head. She will come to us. Trust me.
MID_EV13_060_m01_010: How can you be so certain she will come in person?
MID_EV13_060_m01_011: This is the cornerstone of Saramis's defenses. We\nmay as well have spit directly in her eye.
MID_EV13_060_m01_012: If we put my dear sister down here, chaos will reign,\nand Saramis will collapse.
MID_EV13_060_m01_013: Then I get to make my triumphant return to Megaira\nas the one true king. Hyehehe... HYAHAHA!
MID_EV13_060_m01_014: Our enemy will be here before you know it. I should\ngo prepare for battle.
MID_EV13_060_m01_015: You just sit back and bear witness to the greatness of\nDyan Sergio Savangren.
MID_EV13_060_m01_016: I loathe that man. His self-regard knows no bounds.
MID_EV13_060_m01_017: The way he blew up at me rivaled the eruptions of\nMount Gagorib.
MID_EV13_060_m01_018: I don't understand, General Klapka. Why must we\ndo as he commands?
MID_EV13_060_m01_019: I am told that he was imprisoned in a fortress on\nCottus Island until very recently.
MID_EV13_060_m01_020: The one way out in Saraminian waters?
MID_EV13_060_m01_021: After his allies helped him escape, they took him\nto Mosa soil.
MID_EV13_060_m01_022: There, he demanded a meeting with King Oktar\nand told our liege quite a tale.
MID_EV13_060_m01_023: He claims to be the true king of Saramis, whose\nthrone was usurped by a traitor.
MID_EV13_060_m01_024: In return for helping him, he promised to gladly give\nus Fort Zanbar.
MID_EV13_060_m01_025: And that was all it took for King Oktar to trust him?
MID_EV13_060_m01_026: The king gets bored easily. He found the extent of\nDyan's self-regard amusing.
MID_EV13_060_m01_027: So he gave Dyan all the soldiers he wanted and\nordered me to Fort Zanbar as his aide.
MID_EV13_060_m01_028: I suspect no one was more surprised by our decisive\nvictory the other day than the king.
MID_EV13_060_m01_029: And you really don't mind marching under this\nman's banner, General?
MID_EV13_060_m01_030: Between us, my secondary orders were to cut him\ndown if he ever shows signs of betraying the Mosa.
MID_EV13_060_m01_031: He has no idea how the troops see him or what it\ntakes to be a real king.
MID_EV13_060_m01_032: Watching the man has given me some very sober\nthoughts on how not to be him.
MID_EV13_060_m01_033: His delusions of grandeur have him convinced that\nhe's a god. I only pray he's not all of our deaths.
MID_EV13_061_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_061_m01_001: I have heard how Fort Zanbar fell. So he spread\nmisinformation and used a hidden passage, did he?
MID_EV13_061_m01_002: It is the kind of underhanded trick characteristic\nof my brother.
MID_EV13_061_m01_003: My deepest apologies, Your Majesty. I failed to fully\ntrack the movements of the Dyan faction.
MID_EV13_061_m01_004: <NCA>Stop Kumos there.
MID_EV13_061_m01_005: <NCB>Ask for a briefing.
MID_EV13_061_m01_006: <ACA>Now is not the time for recriminations. The greater\nfault is mine for leaving him alive.
MID_EV13_061_m01_007: <ACA>You can apologize once we have cleaned up this\nmess. For now, outline the situation for me.
MID_EV13_061_m01_008: <ACB>It is forgiven. For now, outline the situation for me.
MID_EV13_061_m01_009: According to reports from Grania Stronghold, the\nenemy has not yet budged from the occupied fort.
MID_EV13_061_m01_010: An estimated force of eight thousand soldiers is\namassed there.
MID_EV13_061_m01_011: So they are waiting for us to make a move. That\nbodes ill. Dyan is scheming something.
MID_EV13_061_m01_012: Still, Your Majesty's timely return is a ray of hope.
MID_EV13_061_m01_013: Be that as it may...Fort Zanbar is notoriously\ndifficult to assault. What are our forces?
MID_EV13_061_m01_014: Between the Saronica and Cybeleia regiments,\n14 thousand soldiers are mustered in Megaira.
MID_EV13_061_m01_015: They are ready to move on a moment's notice by the\nqueen's command.
MID_EV13_061_m01_016: Combined with the 4 thousand garrisoned at Grania\nStronghold, our army is roughly 18 thousand strong.
MID_EV13_061_m01_017: That should be sufficient. We shall teach our foes\nan object lesson in how Saramis makes war.
MID_EV13_061_m01_018: I am still concerned whether even those numbers are\nsufficient to take down such a sturdy bastion.
MID_EV13_061_m01_019: Behind Fort Zanbar is a place called\nHeadsman's Rock.
MID_EV13_061_m01_020: It was an ancient execution ground. From there leads\na narrow game trail to the rear of the stronghold.
MID_EV13_061_m01_021: Once our troops are positioned in front of the fort,\nwe will send a strike force through there.
MID_EV13_061_m01_022: What? I never knew of this trail.
MID_EV13_061_m01_023: My long years captaining the forces there were not\nspent idly.
MID_EV13_061_m01_024: Dyan, meanwhile, lived a carefree life in Megaira.\nHe will not know of it.
MID_EV13_061_m01_025: Ah—
MID_EV13_061_m01_026: What is it? Why are you staring at me?
MID_EV13_061_m01_027: Has something in you changed, Your Majesty?\nFor the better, I mean.
MID_EV13_061_m01_028: As if you'd rid yourself of some foul presence.\nI'm glad to see it.
MID_EV13_061_m01_029: Heh. It is a long story. I shall tell it, and many\nothers of our travels, some other day.
MID_EV13_061_m01_030: For now, let us capture Dyan and take back what is\nrightfully ours. For Saramis's future...to arms!
MID_EV13_061_m01_031: Yes, Your Majesty!
MID_EV13_068_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_068_m01_001: Gwahhh... Ooo...
MID_EV13_068_m01_002: How? How could this happen?
MID_EV13_068_m01_003: This is ridiculous. It can't end here! I am the true\nking of Saramis!
MID_EV13_068_m01_004: <NCA>Address Dyan.
MID_EV13_068_m01_005: <NCB>Execute Dyan.
MID_EV13_068_m01_006: <ACA>Is that all you have to say, Dyan? Accept your\ndefeat like the disgraced warlord that you are.
MID_EV13_068_m01_007: <ACA>It was sparing your life after your last coup attempt\nthat led to this sorry state of affairs.
MID_EV13_068_m01_008: <ACA>I will not make that same mistake twice.\nYou die today.
MID_EV13_068_m01_009: <ACA>No... General Klapka, do something! Tell me King\nOktar is sending a legion of reinforcements!
MID_EV13_068_m01_010: <ACA>Sad to say, we have no choice but to surrender.\nLet's try to accept our fates with some dignity.
MID_EV13_068_m01_011: <ACA>Anyone seeking the throne should also be ready to\ndie at any time.
MID_EV13_068_m01_012: <ACA>This queen understands that much.
MID_EV13_068_m01_013: <ACA>But...I did everything right...
MID_EV13_068_m01_014: Put Dyan on the execution block. I will sever his\nhead from his shoulders.
MID_EV13_068_m01_015: No, no, no, I don't want to die! You soldiers there!\nWhy aren't you protecting me?!
MID_EV13_068_m01_016: Stop! Stop this! I'm your brother, aren't I?!
MID_EV13_068_m01_017: Yes, we've been at each other's throats, but envy will\ndo that to a man, my dear sister.
MID_EV13_068_m01_018: Remember the good days! You and I got along so\nwell in our youths!
MID_EV13_068_m01_019: Ah...
MID_EV13_068_m01_020: Look! I made a flower crown for you out of purple\ntrefoil. Here, bend down so I can put it on you.
MID_EV13_068_m01_021: It feels kind of silly... How do I look?
MID_EV13_068_m01_022: You look perfect. Just like a queen.
MID_EV13_068_m01_023: Thank you, Dyan. Does it really suit me so well?
MID_EV13_068_m01_024: Of course! You're incredible. I'll always be proud of\nmy brave older sister.
MID_EV13_068_m01_035: 
MID_EV13_068_m01_025: <NCA>Swing the axe.
MID_EV13_068_m01_036: 
MID_EV13_068_m01_026: Oh no...this is terrible. Poor Prince Dyan.
MID_EV13_068_m01_027: Never mind him. Let us speak of you, who aided his\nescape. Who coaxed him down this path.
MID_EV13_068_m01_028: No doubt you hoped to have Dyan usurp the throne\nso that you might reap the benefits.
MID_EV13_068_m01_029: You egged him on for your own gain so ruthlessly\nthat Dyan began to believe your lies.
MID_EV13_068_m01_030: Of course not! Prince Dyan begged us to help him.
MID_EV13_068_m01_031: We had no choice but to go along with it. We never\nplotted to conquer Saramis or anything of the sort.
MID_EV13_068_m01_032: Years ago, I offered you a second chance. There will\nnot be a third.
MID_EV13_068_m01_033: Bonaventure. Kill them all.
MID_EV13_068_m01_034: It will be done.
MID_EV13_062_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_062_m01_001: Klapka, was it? I am told you are a Mosa general,\nbut we have not yet been properly introduced.
MID_EV13_062_m01_002: Queen Theodora of Saramis. I would prefer our\npositions were reversed for this conversation.
MID_EV13_062_m01_003: My fool of a brother has caused you no end of grief.\nI bear no responsibility for that, but I will spare you.
MID_EV13_062_m01_004: I have investigated you thoroughly. I gather that your\ntroops hold you in high esteem.
MID_EV13_062_m01_005: I also learned that many of the troops we captured\npleaded with us to show you clemency.
MID_EV13_062_m01_006: A leader like that is valuable—as a hostage.
MID_EV13_062_m01_007: The odds are slim that King Oktar will care much\nabout my capture.
MID_EV13_062_m01_008: <NCA>Regard Klapka.
MID_EV13_062_m01_009: <NCB>Deliver your verdict.
MID_EV13_062_m01_010: <ACA>I wonder about that. You needn't be quite so humble.\nI know your worth, at the very least.
MID_EV13_062_m01_011: <ACA>Saramis will use your status, along with the other\nprisoners of war, to negotiate with the Mosa.
MID_EV13_062_m01_012: Take this man to Megaira. Treat him honorably.
MID_EV13_062_m01_013: Ugh.
MID_EV13_062_m01_014: Reclining in your chair, leaning on an elbow with an\nI'm-in-charge attitude... That's the Theodora I know.
MID_EV13_062_m01_015: It's actually kind of comforting to me to imagine you\nbossing other people around.
MID_EV13_062_m01_016: Heh. Is this the "I'm-in-charge" attitude he prefers?
MID_EV13_062_m01_017: I have finished executing the traitors. I shall continue\noverseeing the rest of the aftermath.
MID_EV13_062_m01_018: This affair seems to have taken a considerable toll on\nyou, Your Majesty.
MID_EV13_062_m01_019: The moment before I beheaded him, I had a sudden\nmemory of when we were children.
MID_EV13_062_m01_020: There was a time when he was innocent. The\nthought nearly dulled my blade.
MID_EV13_062_m01_021: Perhaps in the underworld, the two of us can come\nto a better understanding.
MID_EV13_062_m01_022: Haaah...
MID_EV13_062_m01_023: <NCA>Ask for a casualty report.
MID_EV13_062_m01_024: Tell me, Bonaventure. How many were lost in\nthis battle?
MID_EV13_062_m01_025: Nine hundred dead and 25 hundred injured.\nA monumental achievement, I must say.
MID_EV13_062_m01_026: Be generous in our compensation to the injured and\nreparations to the bereaved families.
MID_EV13_062_m01_027: Confiscate the assets and estates of the traitors. The\ngold they fetch should go towards reparations.
MID_EV13_062_m01_028: As you wish. I shall begin soliciting bids from\ntrusted merchants.
MID_EV13_062_m01_029: Bonaventure...
MID_EV13_062_m01_030: Was what we gained today worth the price in blood?
MID_EV13_062_m01_031: Lives were lost today, Your Majesty. But many more\nwould have been forfeit if we did nothing.
MID_EV13_062_m01_032: Your question can only be answered by a higher\npower than I.
MID_EV13_062_m01_033: I suppose you're right.
MID_EV13_063_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_063_m01_001: Thank you for your service in the Mosa affair. That\nshould do much to maintain peace in the south.
MID_EV13_063_m01_002: Your incredible deeds in support of the empire must\nbe properly rewarded.
MID_EV13_063_m01_040: To that end, as Divine Sovereign, I bestow upon you\nthe prestigious title Flame Lord of Dagda.
MID_EV13_063_m01_041: For your ferocity, you will be known by one and all\nas the Breaker of Armies.
MID_EV13_063_m01_042: I, Queen Theodora of Saramis, do humbly accept\nthe title of Flame Lord of Dagda.
MID_EV13_063_m01_003: A tangible reward is also in order.
MID_EV13_063_m01_004: I will grant the wish from the Heroic Games\nthat we spoke of before.
MID_EV13_063_m01_005: You have my unending gratitude.
MID_EV13_063_m01_006: You sought to annex Cybele and restore Yu Phas's\ntemple, correct?
MID_EV13_063_m01_007: I cannot promise it will be done immediately, but I\nswear that I will entrust the land to you in due time.
MID_EV13_063_m01_008: On behalf of Saramis, it moves me to hear this\nfrom you, Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV13_063_m01_009: But on this subject, there is one more boon I would\nask of you.
MID_EV13_063_m01_010: When we restore Yu Phas's temple, I would like\nto invite her daughter, Aurora, there.
MID_EV13_063_m01_011: So that it may be revived as sacred ground of\nSaramis for many years to come.
MID_EV13_063_m01_012: You would invite Aurora?
MID_EV13_063_m01_013: I am truly touched by the devotion that Saramis\nshows to my wife, Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_063_m01_014: I will consider the matter of Aurora. But she will\nhave her own say in the decision.
MID_EV13_063_m01_015: Forgive me for not promising more, but there are\ncertain...family matters to consider.
MID_EV13_063_m01_016: Even a god must play the dutiful father. It is not a\nside of you I expected to see.
MID_EV13_063_m01_017: You have traveled through the Gate of the Gods.\nDid anything strike you about Ahm Lu?
MID_EV13_063_m01_018: In truth, yes. A feeling of dread suffused the entire\nnecropolis.
MID_EV13_063_m01_019: Then you understand. That land is choked by a dense\nshroud which never clears.
MID_EV13_063_m01_020: I know not whether it is the lingering grudge of\nDamascar or an altogether foreign influence.
MID_EV13_063_m01_021: There are two places in imperial territory that none\nmay approach without the permission of the temples.
MID_EV13_063_m01_022: One is Cybele. The other is the forbidden land.\nThey are known as the void regions.
MID_EV13_063_m01_023: Both those lands are deeply connected to my people.\nAre we feeling the effects of long-ago causes?
MID_EV13_063_m01_024: It was Dagda the Great himself who decreed Cybele\nto be one of the void regions.
MID_EV13_063_m01_025: But his reasons for doing so are known only to him.
MID_EV13_063_m01_026: It was considered disrespectful to the emperor to\npry into his true intentions.
MID_EV13_063_m01_027: But as I have promised this to you, I now have a\nreason to dispatch investigators to that land.
MID_EV13_063_m01_028: I ask that you wait until that investigation is\ncomplete before I grant your wish.
MID_EV13_063_m01_029: Very well.
MID_EV13_063_m01_030: The threat of the Mosa has passed, no? Can you\nnot spare a little time to relax?
MID_EV13_063_m01_031: That is a kind offer, but Saramis is still in turmoil.
MID_EV13_063_m01_032: Between sentencing supporters of the insurrection,\nrecompense for the wounded and dead...
MID_EV13_063_m01_033: repairs and renovations to Fort Zanbar, hostage\nnegotiations with the Mosa...
MID_EV13_063_m01_034: there is a mountain of things my court is keen for\nme to make decisions on.
MID_EV13_063_m01_035: But there is no better parting gift I can take back to\nmy people than your promise, Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV13_063_m01_036: I see your will is as resolute as ever. Once again,\nQueen Theodora, thank you for all you have done.
MID_EV13_063_m01_037: I look forward to the continued prosperity of Saramis.
MID_EV13_063_m01_038: As do I. The Dagdan Empire and kingdom of\nSaramis part this day as friends.
MID_EV13_063_m01_039: May they remain so forever.
MID_NR13_01_m01: <SH>
MID_NR13_01_m01_001: Theodora returned to Megaira and busied herself\nfor days on end with the War of Zanbar's aftermath.
MID_NR13_01_m01_002: With General Klapka as a hostage, Theodora secured\na favorable peace treaty with King Oktar of the\nMosa. Then at long last, her war seemed all but won.
MID_NR13_01_m01_003: But the young queen still had no way of knowing that\nan even greater conflict was about to engulf all of\nDagda. She would find herself in a vortex of\nevents—this time, at its very center.
MID_NR13_01_m01_004: —Saint Cichol, "Fearsome Warriors,"\nPart 3, Chapter 12